1:["$","$Ld",null,{"page":{"id":"phase-4","kind":"phase-index","route":"/roadmap/phase-4","sourceUrl":"https://refold.la/roadmap/phase-4","sourceHash":"60d1783e1c146505d514c307acc02017ba1fe5544adf81c38cf142d7068c6eff","collectedAt":"2026-09-01T23:11:52.182Z","bodyMode":"authorized-full-body","title":{"en":"Speaking","zh":"口语"},"description":{"en":"","zh":""},"segments":[{"id":"segment-0001","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"This is the phase many learners have been waiting for — you're finally going to start speaking. But you might be surprised: after hundreds of hours of input, your first words will come out more naturally than you expect. You already know thousands of words, you understand native speakers, and you've internalized many of the patterns of the language. The main challenge now is building the \"brain to mouth\" connection.","zh":"这是许多学习者一直期待的阶段——你终于要开始说话了。但你可能会感到惊讶：经过数百小时的输入后，你说出的第一句话会比预想中更自然。你已经掌握了数千个词，能够理解母语者，也已经内化了许多语言模式。现在最大的挑战，是建立“从大脑到嘴巴”的连接。"}},{"id":"segment-0002","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"There's an important gap you'll notice immediately: the difference between what you can understand and what you can produce. You'll hear your own mistakes, your awkward phrasing, your pronunciation issues — because your ear is far more advanced than your mouth. This is completely normal. It's actually a <em>good</em> thing, because it means you have a built-in error detector that will help you improve. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/the-input-output-gap\">The Input-Output Gap</a>","zh":"你会立刻注意到一个重要差距：你能理解的内容与能输出的内容之间存在差异。你会听见自己的错误、别扭的措辞和发音问题——因为你的耳朵远比你的嘴巴更先进。这完全正常。事实上，这是一件<em>好</em>事，因为这意味着你拥有一个内置的错误检测器，能够帮助你进步。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/the-input-output-gap\">输入与输出的差距</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0003","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The Refold approach to speaking follows a specific model: Comfort first, then Accuracy. You need to be able to get your thoughts out before you can worry about getting them out <em>correctly</em>. Trying to be accurate before you're comfortable leads to overthinking, hesitation, and a worse experience for everyone. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/the-cara-model-for-output\">The CARA Model for Output</a>","zh":"Refold 的口语方法遵循一个特定模式：先追求舒适，再追求准确。在担心能否说得<em>正确</em>之前，你需要先能够表达自己的想法。在感到舒适之前就试图做到准确，会导致过度思考、犹豫，也会让所有人的体验变差。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/the-cara-model-for-output\">输出的 CARA 模型</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0004","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"By the end of Phase 4, you'll be able to have a real conversation with a native speaker. You'll still make mistakes, but you'll be communicating. Roughly equivalent to B1.","zh":"到第4阶段结束时，你将能够与母语者进行真正的对话。你仍然会犯错，但已经能够进行交流。大致相当于B1水平。"}},{"id":"segment-0005","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Check out Ben's video he made about speaking Czech for the first time after 1000 hours of learning:","zh":"可以看看 Ben 制作的视频：他在学习1000小时后第一次说捷克语："}},{"id":"youtube-G89JMj1_BTQ","type":"embed","src":"https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/G89JMj1_BTQ","title":{"en":"YouTube video","zh":"YouTube 视频"}},{"id":"hour-estimates","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Hour Estimates","zh":"时间估算"}},{"id":"segment-0007","type":"table","rows":[[{"en":"","zh":"","header":true},{"en":"Cousin","zh":"近亲语言","header":true},{"en":"Similar","zh":"相似语言","header":true},{"en":"Neutral","zh":"中性语言","header":true},{"en":"Distant","zh":"远亲语言","header":true}],[{"en":"This phase","zh":"本阶段","header":false},{"en":"90","zh":"90","header":false},{"en":"150","zh":"150","header":false},{"en":"200","zh":"200","header":false},{"en":"300","zh":"300","header":false}],[{"en":"Cumulative","zh":"累计","header":false},{"en":"530","zh":"530","header":false},{"en":"900","zh":"900","header":false},{"en":"1100","zh":"1100","header":false},{"en":"1800","zh":"1800","header":false}]]},{"id":"sub-phases","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Sub-phases","zh":"子阶段"}},{"id":"segment-0009","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>4A — Preparing for Output:</strong> Build the physical and mental foundation for speaking through chorusing, reading aloud, and monologuing.","zh":"<strong>4A — 准备输出：</strong>通过跟读、朗读和独白，为口语建立身体和心理基础。"}},{"id":"segment-0010","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>4B — Speaking Comfort:</strong> Get comfortable speaking through lots of conversation practice. Mistakes don't matter yet — volume does.","zh":"<strong>4B — 口语舒适度：</strong>通过大量对话练习，逐渐适应说话。现在还不用在意错误——练习量才重要。"}},{"id":"segment-0011","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>4X (Optional) — Situational Speaking:</strong> Practice using the language in specific real-life situations (travel, work, daily life). Can be done at any point or skipped entirely.","zh":"<strong>4X（可选）——情境口语：</strong>练习在具体的现实情境中使用语言（旅行、工作、日常生活）。可以在任何时候进行，也可以完全跳过。"}},{"id":"research-and-reasoning","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Research and Reasoning","zh":"研究与依据"}},{"id":"segment-0013","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The input-output gap described here is supported by <a href=\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-92210-7_6\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Swain's (1985)</a> Output Hypothesis, which argues that production serves distinct functions beyond comprehension — it forces learners to notice gaps in their knowledge, test hypotheses about the language, and engage in deeper syntactic processing than comprehension alone requires.","zh":"这里所描述的输入与输出差距得到了<a href=\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-92210-7_6\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Swain（1985）</a>输出假说的支持。该假说认为，语言产出除了理解之外还具有独特作用——它迫使学习者注意到知识缺口，检验关于语言的假设，并进行仅靠理解无法要求的更深层句法加工。"}},{"id":"segment-0014","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The \"Comfort first, then Accuracy\" sequencing reflects the Refold CARA model. The rationale draws on multiple research strands. However, attempting accuracy before you're comfortable speaking at all leads to overthinking and hesitation, as learners try to monitor their output for correctness while simultaneously retrieving words and constructing sentences. By delaying accuracy-focused work until Phase 5, the roadmap ensures that learners first build fluency and procedural knowledge through volume and practice, then layer on monitoring and correction once the basic speaking skill is in place. As long as accuracy does become a focus, bad habits and frequent errors will not fossilize.","zh":"“先追求舒适，再追求准确”的顺序体现了 Refold 的 CARA 模型。这一依据来自多个研究方向。不过，在完全适应说话之前就试图追求准确，会导致过度思考和犹豫，因为学习者需要一边提取词语、构造句子，一边监控输出是否正确。路线图将准确性训练推迟到第5阶段，确保学习者先通过大量练习建立流利度和程序性知识，再在基本口语技能形成后加入监控和纠错。只要之后确实将准确性作为重点，坏习惯和频繁错误就不会固化。"}}],"cards":[{"href":"/roadmap/phase-4/4a-preparing-for-output","title":{"en":"4APreparing for Output","zh":"4A准备输出"}},{"href":"/roadmap/phase-4/4b-speaking-comfort","title":{"en":"4BSpeaking Comfort","zh":"4B口语舒适度"}},{"href":"/roadmap/phase-4/4x-optional-situational-speaking","title":{"en":"4XSituational Speaking","zh":"4X情境口语"}}]}}]
